  "id": "Compound::DB01392 - Gene::150",
  "verbalization": "Yohimbine is implicated in the regulation of alpha-2 adrenergic receptor activity through its interaction with Adra2c, which is a paralog of Adra2a. This binding leads to the activation of the Adrenaline Signalling Through Alpha-2 Adrenergic Receptor pathway, which is ultimately associated with Adra2a. The evidence from the three paths collectively suggests that Yohimbine exerts its effects by modulating the activity of Adra2c, which in turn influences Adra2a through a shared pathway. The varying scores in the paths reflect the strength of the interactions, with the highest confidence in the connection between Yohimbine and Adra2c, and subsequently to Adra2a. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Yohimbine may influence alpha-2 adrenergic signaling, emphasizing the role of Adra2c in mediating its effects on Adra2a.",
